\"--row-id is documented for both modes but unused in session mode.\",\"id\":\"SL-305\",\"linkedFindingId\":\"iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode\",\"rationale\":\"The flag is silently accepted where it cannot narrow anything.\",\"searchActions\":[{\"evidenceRefs\":[\"README.md:112\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:1455\"],\"method\":\"direct_read\",\"queryOrPath\":\"README.md:40,112; score-command-transcripts.mjs:92-95,1433-1455,885-901\",\"result\":\"flag parsed then ignored; scoreSession never reads options.rowId\"}],\"targetRefs\":[\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\",\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\"]},{\"bugClass\":\"documentation_drift\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\",\"hypothesis\":\"NC-011's deep-loop gate is stale after the pass-one attach fix.\",\"id\":\"SL-306\",\"rationale\":\"Expected signals still match the fixed gate.\",\"ruledOutReason\":\"chapter holds\",\"searchActions\":[{\"evidenceRefs\":[\"hub-command-attachment.md:78-90\"],\"method\":\"direct_read\",\"queryOrPath\":\"hub-command-attachment.md:60-90; command-attach.ts:356-366\",\"result\":\"topic prompt no command, depth prompt command; triage symbols resolve\"}],\"targetRefs\":[\"manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md\"]},{\"bugClass\":\"corpus_integrity\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\",\"hypothesis\":\"A corpus grew duplicates or changed size under its gate.\",\"id\":\"SL-307\",\"rationale\":\"Counts and ids are intact.\",\"ruledOutReason\":\"no duplicate or missing id\",\"searchActions\":[{\"evidenceRefs\":[\"labeled-prompts.jsonl\",\"holdout-prompts.jsonl\",\"ambiguity-prompts.jsonl\",\"doctor-prompts.jsonl\"],\"method\":\"corpus_count_tally\",\"queryOrPath\":\"id uniqueness and row counts for the four corpora\",\"result\":\"195/66/24/78 rows, all ids unique\"}],\"targetRefs\":[\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/labeled-prompts.jsonl\",\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl\"]}],\"sessionId\":\"fanout-accuracy-runner-2-1794570021136-noekp0\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"targetSelection\":{\"discoveryMethods\":[\"direct_read\",\"exact_search\",\"numeric_reconciliation\",\"tree_listing\"],\"evidenceRefs\":[\"review-scope-2.txt:103-205\"],\"graphStatus\":\"unavailable\",\"omittedHighRiskTargets\":[\"holdout prompt text (counts only by instruction)\"],\"selectedTargets\":[\"command-routing-baseline.json\",\"scorer-eval-baseline.json\",\"README.md\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\"runtime/tests/README.md\",\"manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts\",\"manual-testing-playbook.md\",\"hub-command-attachment.md\",\"system-skill-advisor/README.md\",\"ARCHITECTURE.md\"],\"selectionReason\":\"Every area file whose claim names a number, a path or a test description, plus the shared docs that describe the harness.\",\"semanticSearchStatus\":\"unavailable\"},\"target_agent\":\"deep-review\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-13T12:10:00Z\",\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"agent_cross_runtime\":{\"notes\":\"Per-runtime proof remains phase 007.\",\"status\":\"partial\"},\"checklist_evidence\":{\"notes\":\"No parent checklist; phase 007 open rows remain the closure gap.\",\"status\":\"partial\"},\"feature_catalog_code\":{\"notes\":\"advisor-recommend.md links NC-001/004/005 and matches area semantics.\",\"status\":\"pass\"},\"playbook_capability\":{\"notes\":\"NC-011 holds; root playbook inventory and persistence statements do not.\",\"status\":\"partial\"},\"skill_agent\":{\"notes\":\"No owner agent.\",\"status\":\"notApplicable\"},\"spec_code\":{\"notes\":\"All five pinned numbers re-derived; pinned clock matches scorer-eval baseline.\",\"status\":\"pass\"}},\"type\":\"iteration\"}\n---STRATEGY---\n# Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-2 Lineage\n\n## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder target)\n- Fan-out lineage: `accuracy-runner-2` (artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2`); pass-two area is `accuracy-runner`\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n- Stop conditions: legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold=0.10`, or `maxIterations=7`, whichever comes first\n- Success criteria: every pass-one finding in the area re-verified; every file marked `yes` in `review-scope-2.txt` reviewed line by line; every area file covered at least once; findings carry `file:line` and a concrete input; holdout hygiene verified by counts only\n- Review focus (operator bound): pass-two code review of command surfacing. Re-verify each pass-one fix in the area, review every file changed since pass one line by line for a defect the fix introduced, then look for new defects. Check behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code.\n- Resource map: `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate\n- Baseline: pass one is closed at `review/review-report-pass-1.md`; its fixes landed in `b3b5ae8314` and `3b48f0e5f1`\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nCommand surfacing behaviour for the routed skill/command advisor, restricted to the `accuracy-runner` area: the routing-accuracy measurement harness (`runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/`), the prompt corpora and their committed baselines, the cost-measurement benches, the transcript/offer tests, the legacy fidelity tests and the manual-testing playbook that documents how to run them.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n[All dimensions complete]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin` or `doctor-install` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n- Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n- Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n- Not re-reporting a pass-one finding whose fix holds, the deferred items in report section 8, `R4-P2-003`, or the refuted finding\n- Not running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage; runners are audited by reading, and only the single-file vitest commands the dispatch allows were run\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n- `maxIterations=7` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n- Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n- [x] traceability\n- [x] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 12\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Re-reading each fix at its cited line and then running the two guard files turned the fix replay into observed evidence instead of a doc comparison (iteration 1).\n- Counting the corpus and baseline by `id`, `split` and `row_type` proved holdout hygiene without ever printing prompt text (iteration 1).\n- Asking \"which caller reaches this line\" found the g2 `--row-id` arm defect: the selection code and `armFor` disagree only on a path neither file's comment covers (iteration 2).\n- Reading `finally` against every mutation the `try` makes found that only the clock and the temp directory are restored, not the environment (iteration 2).\n- Re-deriving every spec floor from the committed baseline turned traceability into arithmetic, and all five floors held (iteration 4).\n- Comparing each doc line with the tree or the function it names exposed two playbook statements and one test-table description that a green gate cannot catch (iteration 4).\n- A local `git init` probe turned the porcelain quoting question into an observed fact instead of a guess, which is what raised the restore finding from suspicion to evidence (iteration 5).\n- Replaying every active finding before the final iteration kept the terminal counts honest and closed the coverage map without a new finding (iteration 6-7).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- The phase-map fix cannot be confirmed from the parent map: its reason sits only in `007/tasks.md`, so the pass-one item is reported again rather than closed (iteration 1).\n- An early suspicion that `parseOffer` swallows a trailing word failed the reach test: the renderer never prints a bare word after the command, so it stays ruled out rather than a finding (iteration 2).\n- A first read of the playbook's \"41 `NNN-*.md`\" note looked like a missing-file report; the tree shows 50 differently named files, so the finding was narrowed to the note (iteration 4).\n- A first read of the legacy parity comment looked like it contradicted its accepted list; the list's own \"reviewed-accepted divergence\" wording resolved it, so it stayed ruled out (iteration 5).\n- The coverage graph was unavailable in every iteration, so the loop could not claim a legal graph-backed STOP and stopped at the cap instead (iteration 7).\n\n---\n\n[showing lines 23-219 of 219; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1daa1130e001lj3ay8jadtJacv.out]","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":true,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-13T11:48:49Z\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"cli-opencode\",\n    \"model\": \"opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\n    \"reasoningEffort\": \"max\",\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": \"danger-full-access\",\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewFocus\": \"Code review of command surfacing, PASS TWO. First read the full instructions in the pass-two instructions file and follow them: for each pass-one finding in the accuracy-runner area, re-read the code and say whether the fix holds; review every file marked yes (changed since pass one) line by line for a defect the fix introduced; then look for new defects. Scope file lists area, path and changed-since-pass-one. Check behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. Change no code, write only inside the lineage folder.\",\n  \"resource_map_present\": false,\n  \"resource_map\": {\n    \"emit\": true\n  },\n  \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n  \"crossReference\": {\n    \"core\": [\n      \"spec_code\",\n      \"checklist_evidence\"\n    ],\n    \"overlay\": [\n      \"skill_agent\",\n      \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n      \"feature_catalog_code\",\n      \"playbook_capability\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2\",\n  \"fanoutLineageLabe