{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669661218,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa5c66c001Ii93I5eftgc16z","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1daa4bf0d001p9WRh8YyRVw8Ad","type":"tool","id":"call_fd544e71ef304d6098ad462f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"commandOwner\\|plain_stages\\|ownerLed\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts; echo \"---README new---\"; git diff 0cdc9fa3ef..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -160"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:358:  return { total: 0, own: 0, ownerLed: 0, routed: 0, withCommand: 0, attached: 0, neither: 0 };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:364:  if (facts.ownerLed) tally.ownerLed += 1;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:500:    const commandOwner = new Map();\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:502:      commandOwner.set(entry.command, entry.skillId);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:636:        // `own` and `ownerLed` split the rows and `neither` is the remainder,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:638:        const owningSkill = expected === null ? undefined : commandOwner.get(expected);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:639:        const ownerLed = !top1Hit && owningSkill !== undefined && owningSkill === topId;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:640:        const routed = ownerLed && route !== undefined;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:644:          ownerLed,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:648:          neither: !top1Hit && !ownerLed,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:760:        plain_stages: {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:68:  readonly ownerLed: number;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:224:      readonly plain_stages: Readonly<Record<'tune' | 'holdout', StageTally>>;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:227:      const stage = attached.plain_stages[split];\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:228:      expect(stage.own + stage.ownerLed + stage.neither).toBe(stage.total);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:231:      expect(stage.routed).toBeLessThanOrEqual(stage.ownerLed);\n---README new---\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\nindex a9922d76d0..36dab643bb 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -101,6 +101,14 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n - Refusal: a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor.\n - Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. Each hook process also runs without `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so a run from a dispatched worker measures the brief an operator's own session receives rather than the child form. Each hook child runs with `TMPDIR` set to the sandbox, so a cost run writes no health record into the shared metrics folder. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\n \n+### Reading the outcome\n+\n+- A loaded document is not a followed step, so `loadRate` and `followedRange` say a workflow opened, not that its steps were taken.\n+- The behaviour rows are tuned rows, so `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` describe the corpus the brief was built against, not a fresh one.\n+- Each row ran once, so one run moves a rate by more than the range around it can settle.\n+- Two arms differ in more than the brief, so a `--pair` gain or loss is not the brief's effect alone.\n+- The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, so the split by offer says what the Claude head carried for that row.\n+\n ---\n \n ## 4. STRUCTURE\n@@ -110,9 +118,9 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `gate3-corpus-runner.mjs` | MJS source file in this folder. |\n | `score-routing-corpus.py` | PY source file in this folder. |\n | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt corpus with a gold slash command per row, covering every tracked command. |\n-| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. |\n-| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n-| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. |\n+| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Three of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 5 of 8. |\n+| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n | `build-holdout.mjs` | Builds the frozen holdout from three separately authored fixtures that are disjoint from the labeled corpus, copying each row's own label and keeping its provenance in `source_type` and `origin_fixture`. Family-normalized dedup keeps the first occurrence and drops any prompt that collides with the training corpus. `--write` rewrites `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:358:  return { total: 0, own: 0, ownerLed: 0, routed: 0, withCommand: 0, attached: 0, neither: 0 };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:364:  if (facts.ownerLed) tally.ownerLed += 1;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:500:    const commandOwner = new Map();\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:502:      commandOwner.set(entry.command, entry.skillId);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:636:        // `own` and `ownerLed` split the rows and `neither` is the remainder,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:638:        const owningSkill = expected === null ? undefined : commandOwner.get(expected);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:639:        const ownerLed = !top1Hit && owningSkill !== undefined && owningSkill === topId;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:640:        const routed = ownerLed && route !== undefined;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:644:          ownerLed,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:648:          neither: !top1Hit && !ownerLed,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:760:        plain_stages: {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:68:  readonly ownerLed: number;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:224:      readonly plain_stages: Readonly<Record<'tune' | 'holdout', StageTally>>;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:227:      const stage = attached.plain_stages[split];\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:228:      expect(stage.own + stage.ownerLed + stage.neither).toBe(stage.total);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:231:      expect(stage.routed).toBeLessThanOrEqual(stage.ownerLed);\n---README new---\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\nindex a9922d76d0..36dab643bb 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -101,6 +101,14 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n - Refusal: a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor.\n - Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. Each hook process also runs without `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so a run from a dispatched worker measures the brief an operator's own session receives rather than the child form. Each hook child runs with `TMPDIR` set to the sandbox, so a cost run writes no health record into the shared metrics folder. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\n \n+### Reading the outcome\n+\n+- A loaded document is not a followed step, so `loadRate` and `followedRange` say a workflow opened, not that its steps were taken.\n+- The behaviour rows are tuned rows, so `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` describe the corpus the brief was built against, not a fresh one.\n+- Each row ran once, so one run moves a rate by more than the range around it can settle.\n+- Two arms differ in more than the brief, so a `--pair` gain or loss is not the brief's effect alone.\n+- The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, so the split by offer says what the Claude head carried for that row.\n+\n ---\n \n ## 4. STRUCTURE\n@@ -110,9 +118,9 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `gate3-corpus-runner.mjs` | MJS source file in this folder. |\n | `score-routing-corpus.py` | PY source file in this folder. |\n | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt corpus with a gold slash command per row, covering every tracked command. |\n-| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. |\n-| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n-| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. |\n+| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Three of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 5 of 8. |\n+| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n | `build-holdout.mjs` | Builds the frozen holdout from three separately authored fixtures that are disjoint from the labeled corpus, copying each row's own label and keeping its provenance in `source_type` and `origin_fixture`. Family-normalized dedup keeps the first occurrence and drops any prompt that collides with the training corpus. `--write` rewrites `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"commandOwner\\\\|plain_stages\\\\|ownerLed\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts; echo \\\"---README new---\\\"; git diff 0cdc9fa3ef..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -160\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669659756,"end":1794669661218}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669661275,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa5c0d9001CbjQumkEn8SnFp","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1daa4bf0d001p9WRh8YyRVw8Ad","type":"tool","id":"call_a36b620f301e46ed81cbf162","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs; echo \"---bridge sample---\"; node -e \"const j=require('./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json'); console.log(j.entries.slice(0,5)); console.log('entries', j.entries.length); const e=j.entries.find(x=>x.ownerMode); console.log('ownerMode sample', e);\""},"output":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: COMMAND ROUTING BASELINE CAPTURE\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n//\n// Captures how the built scorer routes the command-prompt corpus under the\n// reproducible filesystem projection (empty SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR →\n// SQLite loader returns null → projection built purely from committed graph\n// metadata). It answers the questions command surfacing has to hold to: a\n// prompt that names a slash command reaches that command's bridge, a prompt\n// that must stay quiet offers no command at all, a partial slash mention is\n// not routed as if it were complete, and a bridge ranked below the top skill\n// is owned by that skill.\n//\n// It also measures what the compiled route adds on top of that: a hub can name\n// the slash command its own routing would take, which reaches a reader who never\n// types a slash command. That reach is reported under its own key so every\n// existing number keeps the value and the comparability it had before.\n//\n// The result is the ratchet baseline: the gate re-scores live under the same\n// environment and holds every count to it, so any scoring or bridge-metadata\n// change that moves a number forces a conscious re-capture rather than\n// drifting silently. `corpusSha256` pins the baseline to the exact corpus it\n// was captured against, so a corpus edit changes the hash and forces\n// re-baselining.\n//\n// The same corpus can also be scored against the operator's own skill graph and\n// embedder under `--real-embedding`, which is a live probe of this machine rather\n// than a reproducible projection. Its numbers describe an environment, so it never\n// writes the baseline and never runs under the fixture regime the ratchet replays.\n//\n// Setup runs on call, never on import: the environment projection, the clock\n// pin and the scorer import all live inside scoreCommandCorpus(), so a harness\n// may import this module and score in-process without inheriting either.\n//\n// Usage:\n//   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs            # print JSON to stdout\n//   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write    # also write the baseline\n//   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding   # score live vectors\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { execFileSync, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { existsSync, mkdtempSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { rejectUnknownOptions } from './reject-unknown-options.mjs';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst CORPUS_JSONL = resolve(HERE, 'command-prompts.jsonl');\nconst BRIDGES_JSON = resolve(HERE, '../command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json');\nconst SCORER_EVAL_BASELINE_JSON = resolve(HERE, 'scorer-eval-baseline.json');\nconst OUTPUT_JSON = resolve(HERE, 'command-routing-baseline.json');\nconst DIST = resolve(HERE, '../../dist/runtime');\nconst FUSION_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/scorer/fusion.js');\nconst WORKSPACE_ROOT_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/utils/workspace-root.js');\nconst COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/command-attach.js');\nconst PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js');\nconst COMPILED_ROUTING_FLAG_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/compiled-routing-flag.js');\nconst SEMANTIC_SHADOW_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js');\nconst SKILL_GRAPH_DB_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js');\nconst DIST_FRESHNESS_MODULE = resolve(HERE, '../../../../system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/dist-freshness.cjs');\n\nconst SENTINEL = '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md';\nconst COMMANDS_DIR = '.skilled/commands';\n// Only the folder-level README is a document; a lowercase `readme.md` shipped\n// beside the commands is itself a command, so the skip is case-sensitive.\nconst COMMAND_DOC_SKIP = 'README.md';\nconst COMMAND_DOC_SUFFIX = '.md';\n// The compiled route is asked for through the public front door a hub's SKILL.md\n// calls, so this measures the decision the runtime actually serves rather than a\n// second derivation of it that could disagree with the first.\n---bridge sample---\n[\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-agent',\n    command: '/create:agent',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-agent',\n    description: 'Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'create an OpenCode agent',\n      'define agent permissions',\n      'write an agent persona'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    embeddingText: 'I want to create an OpenCode agent with explicit permissions and behavioral rules. create an OpenCode agent. define agent permissions. write an agent persona',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-benchmark',\n    command: '/create:benchmark',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-benchmark',\n    description: 'Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'author benchmark artifacts',\n      'create a conformance benchmark',\n      'write benchmark fixtures'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-changelog',\n    command: '/create:changelog',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-changelog',\n    description: 'Create a global changelog entry. Topology-aware, optional GitHub release. :auto/:confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'write release notes',\n      'create a packet changelog',\n      'bump a component version'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-command',\n    command: '/create:command',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-command',\n    description: 'Create or update OpenCode slash command sets with :auto/:confirm workflow assets.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'create a slash command',\n      'scaffold command routing',\n      'write command frontmatter'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-diff',\n    command: '/create:diff',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-diff',\n    description: 'Create a self-contained before/after document diff report via the create-diff engine. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'compare document versions',\n      'review a document diff',\n      'make an HTML diff report'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  }\n]\nentries 63\nownerMode sample {\n  id: 'command-create-agent',\n  command: '/create:agent',\n  skillId: 'sk-doc',\n  ownerMode: 'sk-create-agent',\n  description: 'Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n  ownedSignals: [\n    'create an OpenCode agent',\n    'define agent permissions',\n    'write an agent persona'\n  ],\n  standalone: false,\n  mutating: 'mutates',\n  source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n  embeddingText: 'I want to create an OpenCode agent with explicit permissions and behavioral rules. create an OpenCode agent. define agent permissions. write an agent persona',\n  runtime: {\n    typescript: {\n      enabled: true,\n      inventoryId: 'command-create-agent',\n      order: 3,\n      id: 'create:agent',\n      name: 'create:agent',\n      description: 'Create command bridge for /create:agent OpenCode agent scaffolding.',\n      keywords: [Array],\n      domains: [Array],\n      intentSignals: [Array]\n    },\n    python: {\n      enabled: true,\n      inventoryId: 'command-create-agent',\n      order: 10,\n      id: 'command-create-agent',\n      description: 'Create a new OpenCode agent using /create:agent.',\n      slashMarkers: [Array]\n    }\n  }\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: COMMAND ROUTING BASELINE CAPTURE\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n//\n// Captures how the built scorer routes the command-prompt corpus under the\n// reproducible filesystem projection (empty SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR →\n// SQLite loader returns null → projection built purely from committed graph\n// metadata). It answers the questions command surfacing has to hold to: a\n// prompt that names a slash command reaches that command's bridge, a prompt\n// that must stay quiet offers no command at all, a partial slash mention is\n// not routed as if it were complete, and a bridge ranked below the top skill\n// is owned by that skill.\n//\n// It also measures what the compiled route adds on top of that: a hub can name\n// the slash command its own routing would take, which reaches a reader who never\n// types a slash command. That reach is reported under its own key so every\n// existing number keeps the value and the comparability it had before.\n//\n// The result is the ratchet baseline: the gate re-scores live under the same\n// environment and holds every count to it, so any scoring or bridge-metadata\n// change that moves a number forces a conscious re-capture rather than\n// drifting silently. `corpusSha256` pins the baseline to the exact corpus it\n// was captured against, so a corpus edit changes the hash and forces\n// re-baselining.\n//\n// The same corpus can also be scored against the operator's own skill graph and\n// embedder under `--real-embedding`, which is a live probe of this machine rather\n// than a reproducible projection. Its numbers describe an environment, so it never\n// writes the baseline and never runs under the fixture regime the ratchet replays.\n//\n// Setup runs on call, never on import: the environment projection, the clock\n// pin and the scorer import all live inside scoreCommandCorpus(), so a harness\n// may import this module and score in-process without inheriting either.\n//\n// Usage:\n//   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs            # print JSON to stdout\n//   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write    # also write the baseline\n//   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding   # score live vectors\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { execFileSync, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { existsSync, mkdtempSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { rejectUnknownOptions } from './reject-unknown-options.mjs';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst CORPUS_JSONL = resolve(HERE, 'command-prompts.jsonl');\nconst BRIDGES_JSON = resolve(HERE, '../command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json');\nconst SCORER_EVAL_BASELINE_JSON = resolve(HERE, 'scorer-eval-baseline.json');\nconst OUTPUT_JSON = resolve(HERE, 'command-routing-baseline.json');\nconst DIST = resolve(HERE, '../../dist/runtime');\nconst FUSION_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/scorer/fusion.js');\nconst WORKSPACE_ROOT_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/utils/workspace-root.js');\nconst COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/command-attach.js');\nconst PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js');\nconst COMPILED_ROUTING_FLAG_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/compiled-routing-flag.js');\nconst SEMANTIC_SHADOW_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js');\nconst SKILL_GRAPH_DB_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js');\nconst DIST_FRESHNESS_MODULE = resolve(HERE, '../../../../system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/dist-freshness.cjs');\n\nconst SENTINEL = '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md';\nconst COMMANDS_DIR = '.skilled/commands';\n// Only the folder-level README is a document; a lowercase `readme.md` shipped\n// beside the commands is itself a command, so the skip is case-sensitive.\nconst COMMAND_DOC_SKIP = 'README.md';\nconst COMMAND_DOC_SUFFIX = '.md';\n// The compiled route is asked for through the public front door a hub's SKILL.md\n// calls, so this measures the decision the runtime actually serves rather than a\n// second derivation of it that could disagree with the first.\n---bridge sample---\n[\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-agent',\n    command: '/create:agent',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-agent',\n    description: 'Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'create an OpenCode agent',\n      'define agent permissions',\n      'write an agent persona'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    embeddingText: 'I want to create an OpenCode agent with explicit permissions and behavioral rules. create an OpenCode agent. define agent permissions. write an agent persona',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-benchmark',\n    command: '/create:benchmark',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-benchmark',\n    description: 'Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'author benchmark artifacts',\n      'create a conformance benchmark',\n      'write benchmark fixtures'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-changelog',\n    command: '/create:changelog',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-changelog',\n    description: 'Create a global changelog entry. Topology-aware, optional GitHub release. :auto/:confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'write release notes',\n      'create a packet changelog',\n      'bump a component version'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-command',\n    command: '/create:command',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-command',\n    description: 'Create or update OpenCode slash command sets with :auto/:confirm workflow assets.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'create a slash command',\n      'scaffold command routing',\n      'write command frontmatter'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'command-create-diff',\n    command: '/create:diff',\n    skillId: 'sk-doc',\n    ownerMode: 'sk-create-diff',\n    description: 'Create a self-contained before/after document diff report via the create-diff engine. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n    ownedSignals: [\n      'compare document versions',\n      'review a document diff',\n      'make an HTML diff report'\n    ],\n    standalone: false,\n    mutating: 'mutates',\n    source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n    runtime: { typescript: [Object], python: [Object] }\n  }\n]\nentries 63\nownerMode sample {\n  id: 'command-create-agent',\n  command: '/create:agent',\n  skillId: 'sk-doc',\n  ownerMode: 'sk-create-agent',\n  description: 'Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.',\n  ownedSignals: [\n    'create an OpenCode agent',\n    'define agent permissions',\n    'write an agent persona'\n  ],\n  standalone: false,\n  mutating: 'mutates',\n  source: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json',\n  embeddingText: 'I want to create an OpenCode agent with explicit permissions and behavioral rules. create an OpenCode agent. define agent permissions. write an agent persona',\n  runtime: {\n    typescript: {\n      enabled: true,\n      inventoryId: 'command-create-agent',\n      order: 3,\n      id: 'create:agent',\n      name: 'create:agent',\n      description: 'Create command bridge for /create:agent OpenCode agent scaffolding.',\n      keywords: [Array],\n      domains: [Array],\n      intentSignals: [Array]\n    },\n    python: {\n      enabled: true,\n      inventoryId: 'command-create-agent',\n      order: 10,\n      id: 'command-create-agent',\n      description: 'Create a new OpenCode agent using /create:agent.',\n      slashMarkers: [Array]\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs; echo \\\"---bridge sample---\\\"; node -e \\\"const j=require('./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json'); console.log(j.entries.slice(0,5)); console.log('entries', j.entries.length); const e=j.entries.find(x=>x.ownerMode); console.log('ownerMode sample', e);\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669658329,"end":1794669661275}}}}
