{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794670487937,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"id":"prt_1dab2698100182evYiF7TcrY9y","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab257f0001Kxu4mE5bJSYuHV","type":"step-start","snapshot":"df29821aba75438c4bcf3cdd06c5afb8efd061d2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670539155,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab32e63001iKvzqPqkmb9n37","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab257f0001Kxu4mE5bJSYuHV","type":"tool","id":"call_82928ec5674e4f70ad294140","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '55,75p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md; sed -n '180,190p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md; sed -n '1958,1988p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json"},"output":"## 3. FEATURES\n\n| Feature | What It Does |\n|---|---|\n| Folder boundary | Documents direct code files under `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy`. |\n| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling and type-discipline checks. |\n| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n\n### Attribution on every run line\n\nEach line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n\n- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a readable record, and `unknown` where none exists or cannot be read, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n\nThe offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n\n### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n**Backfill a finished log**\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs \\\n  --backfill scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --out scratch/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl\n```\n\nThe output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n\n---\n\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"fit\": {\n      \"skillOnly\": {\n        \"carried\": 0,\n        \"total\": 24\n      },\n      \"decline\": {\n        \"carried\": 8,\n        \"total\": 24,\n        \"byKind\": {\n          \"refusal\": {\n            \"carried\": 3,\n            \"total\": 6\n          },\n          \"question\": {\n            \"carried\": 3,\n            \"total\": 6\n          },\n          \"small-edit\": {\n            \"carried\": 2,\n            \"total\": 6\n          },\n          \"app-problem\": {\n            \"carried\": 0,\n            \"total\": 6\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 3. FEATURES\n\n| Feature | What It Does |\n|---|---|\n| Folder boundary | Documents direct code files under `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy`. |\n| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling and type-discipline checks. |\n| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n\n### Attribution on every run line\n\nEach line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n\n- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a readable record, and `unknown` where none exists or cannot be read, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n\nThe offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n\n### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n**Backfill a finished log**\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs \\\n  --backfill scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --out scratch/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl\n```\n\nThe output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n\n---\n\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"fit\": {\n      \"skillOnly\": {\n        \"carried\": 0,\n        \"total\": 24\n      },\n      \"decline\": {\n        \"carried\": 8,\n        \"total\": 24,\n        \"byKind\": {\n          \"refusal\": {\n            \"carried\": 3,\n            \"total\": 6\n          },\n          \"question\": {\n            \"carried\": 3,\n            \"total\": 6\n          },\n          \"small-edit\": {\n            \"carried\": 2,\n            \"total\": 6\n          },\n          \"app-problem\": {\n            \"carried\": 0,\n            \"total\": 6\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '55,75p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md; sed -n '180,190p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md; sed -n '1958,1988p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670538339,"end":1794670539155}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670539166,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab329df0010szlW5uR3wn5lB","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab257f0001Kxu4mE5bJSYuHV","type":"tool","id":"call_b2931447d29e4612afbdcf41","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ; echo \"---verify lines---\"; sed -n '1460,1475p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs; sed -n '486,500p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs; sed -n '1178,1190p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs"},"output":"2026-11-14T15:35:39Z\n---verify lines---\n// command instead of being read as a refusal. An ambiguous head names two paths and\n// only the first leads, so a command on the partner side was shown and not offered,\n// and a line written before the field existed keeps its count because where its\n// command sat is unknown.\nfunction offerOf(line, label) {\n  const hasOffer = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(line, 'offeredCommand');\n  const wanted = commandParts(label.expected_command);\n  return {\n    offered: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n    partner: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n    offerFieldAbsent: !hasOffer,\n  };\n}\n\n    let nextLine;\n    if (briefOnly) {\n      nextLine = { ...line, briefDelivered: delivered, briefBackfilled: true };\n    } else {\n      nextLine = {\n        ...line,\n        offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null,\n        offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,\n        offerError: offer.offerError ?? null,\n        briefDelivered: delivered,\n        offerBackfilled: true,\n      };\n    }\n    output.push(nextLine);\n  }\n  // Pi, Devin and DSH keep the brief in their session store rather than in the\n  // turn records, so the delivery check needs the reader that opens that store.\n  const delivered = options.dryRun\n    ? 'unknown'\n    : await briefDelivered({ runtime: job.runtimeName, locator, loadSession: loadSharedSession });\n  appendRunLine(options.out, {\n    ...line,\n    offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand,\n    offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,\n    briefDelivered: delivered,\n    restored,\n    ...(restore !== null && restore.leftoverPaths.length > 0\n      ? { leftoverPaths: restore.leftoverPaths }\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2026-11-14T15:35:39Z\n---verify lines---\n// command instead of being read as a refusal. An ambiguous head names two paths and\n// only the first leads, so a command on the partner side was shown and not offered,\n// and a line written before the field existed keeps its count because where its\n// command sat is unknown.\nfunction offerOf(line, label) {\n  const hasOffer = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(line, 'offeredCommand');\n  const wanted = commandParts(label.expected_command);\n  return {\n    offered: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n    partner: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n    offerFieldAbsent: !hasOffer,\n  };\n}\n\n    let nextLine;\n    if (briefOnly) {\n      nextLine = { ...line, briefDelivered: delivered, briefBackfilled: true };\n    } else {\n      nextLine = {\n        ...line,\n        offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null,\n        offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,\n        offerError: offer.offerError ?? null,\n        briefDelivered: delivered,\n        offerBackfilled: true,\n      };\n    }\n    output.push(nextLine);\n  }\n  // Pi, Devin and DSH keep the brief in their session store rather than in the\n  // turn records, so the delivery check needs the reader that opens that store.\n  const delivered = options.dryRun\n    ? 'unknown'\n    : await briefDelivered({ runtime: job.runtimeName, locator, loadSession: loadSharedSession });\n  appendRunLine(options.out, {\n    ...line,\n    offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand,\n    offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,\n    briefDelivered: delivered,\n    restored,\n    ...(restore !== null && restore.leftoverPaths.length > 0\n      ? { leftoverPaths: restore.leftoverPaths }\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ; echo \\\"---verify lines---\\\"; sed -n '1460,1475p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs; sed -n '486,500p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs; sed -n '1178,1190p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670537183,"end":1794670539166}}}}
