{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794670574106,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"id":"prt_1dab3ba1a001TmhHShO4uiyq8L","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab3aa180010ky3d41zu2xn7T","type":"step-start","snapshot":"643b0c073c7abaa217a33450637136f3e3b9a933"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670628011,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab40b85001FvyCrx6elSVfCU","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab3aa180010ky3d41zu2xn7T","type":"tool","id":"call_06ba9d6b4f4244eb8c2e45a1","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-4`, pass four)\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Dimension: D1 Correctness, first pass over the area changed since pass three\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Budget profile: verify (12 review actions)\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: pass-four review of command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area. Read `review-brief-4.txt` first; review the files whose area is `accuracy-runner` plus shared docs; check the six runtimes, whether a refusal/question/mention can attach or start a mutating command, whether the transcript scorer counts a load/followed step/offer that did not happen (Codex exec bodies, rg/grep, heredocs, cd, partner-side commands, paired arms, Wilson ranges), holdout hygiene, and docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text.\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it read the two pass-four producer changes (`command-offer.mjs` and the `4a622e419f` offer field) against their consumer (`score-command-transcripts.mjs`), then read the `a1c31b6f38` Codex/heredoc/`cd` reader and its tests. It found the partner-side offer field that is computed and then dropped before any run line reaches the scorer, a heredoc delimiter the new shell reader leaves in the command stream, and a shell read the new path counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop. Holdout rows were counted only; no holdout prompt text was printed.\n- `steer.md`: absent before this iteration; no lead rulings to apply.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:52-80,99-147,486-499`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1177-1190` (read-only producer context; unchanged since pass three)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:643-693,718-748,913-926,975-990,1430-1438,1464-1474`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:58-72,123,187`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:73-113,305-350`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:177-275,2199-2252`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (ids, splits and row types only; no holdout prompt text)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **The partner-side offer field is computed and then dropped by both offer writers** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:486` -- `parseOffer` and `replayOffer` return `offeredAs` (`head` or `partner`), and the scorer's `offerOf` uses it to keep a command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head out of `offered` (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1464-1473`). No writer persists that field. `backfillRunLog` copies only `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled` into the new line (`command-offer.mjs:490-497`). The live runner's `appendRunLine` copies only `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` from the same replay (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187`). A real backfilled or live run line therefore has no `offeredAs`, and `offerOf` reads `undefined !== 'partner'` as `offered: true`. The README says \"Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`\" (`README.md:123`) and separately lists the output fields without it (`README.md:187`), so the docs disagree with each other and with both writers.\nFinding class: correctness / cross-consumer\nScope proof: `rg -n \"offeredAs\"` over the runtime shows the only producers are `failedOffer`, `parseOffer` and `replayOffer`, the only consumer is `offerOf`, and both write paths that call `replayOffer` select fields without it. `command-offer.vitest.ts:337-350`'s replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so the backfill test cannot catch the drop.\nAffected surface hints: `command-offer.mjs` `backfillRunLog`; `run-command-behaviour.mjs` `appendRunLine`; `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `offerOf`; README \"Attribution on every run line\" and \"Backfill a finished log\".\nCase: a run whose head is `Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-code 0.95/0.12 vs sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.82/0.12 pass.` gets `offeredAs: 'partner'` from `replayOffer`; the line written by the runner or a backfill has no `offeredAs`; the scorer counts `/create:manual-testing-playbook` as `offered` and leaves `offeredAsPartner` at 0, so `startedOfOffered` and `followedOffered` treat a command the head showed on the partner side as an offer the head made.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"claim\",\n  \"claim\": \"The partner-side offer marker is added by parseOffer/replayOffer but is not copied into any run line by either producer, so the scorer's partner-side exclusion never fires on a real log.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:70-81\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:486-497\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1464-1473\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:187\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Searched every runtime file for another writer of offeredAs (none); checked whether run-command-behaviour spreads the whole replay object (it selects two fields); checked whether the scorer can infer the partner side from offeredCommand alone (the same string can be head or partner); checked whether the backfill test's stub returns offeredAs (it does not).\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The field could be intended only for the scorer's unit tests and for a future producer, in which case the README claim and the scorer's read are the defects rather than the writers.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.95,\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"If every run log is normalized to add offeredAs before scoring, or the scorer derives the partner side from a stored head, this becomes a P2 documentation cleanup.\"\n}\n```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:647` -- `HEREDOC_BODY` matches a delimiter with `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*` only. A quoted delimiter with a hyphen, such as `END-SCRIPT`, is not matched, so the body stays in the command stream and `shellReadTargets` parses its lines as commands. A body line that names a workflow document then counts as a load the run never performed. The only heredoc tests use `EOF` (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:2222-2223`).\nFinding class: correctness / measurement\nScope proof: the regex is the only heredoc filter, `shellReadTargets` is the only shell reader, and both `followedBeforeWrite` and `ownerLoadedBeforeWrite` consume its targets. No test uses a delimiter outside the identifier grammar.\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `HEREDOC_BODY`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` heredoc cases.\nCase: a Codex or Claude shell step runs `python3 - <<'END-SCRIPT'` with a body line `cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` and then writes; the body is data, but `shellReadTargets` returns the `SKILL.md` target and `workflowPath` reports `skill` although the file was never opened.\n\n2. **A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:913` -- The pass-four shell-read support is wired into `followedBeforeWrite` (`:734-736`) and `ownerLoadedBeforeWrite` (`:793`), but `readDocument` still accepts only `read` and `skill` events (`:916-923`). `startState` therefore reports `started: false` for a Codex run that `cat`s the command document, and `takenLoop` (`:1430-1438`) cannot name a loop opened the same way, so a deep-loop run that reads its document through the shell and writes without its init is not marked unsafe.\nFinding class: correctness / measurement\nScope proof: `readDocument` is the single start/loop detector; the new shell readers are the only way a Codex `exec` body becomes a load; no test combines a shell read with `startState` or `takenLoop`.\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `readDocument`, `startState`, `takenLoop`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` start and loop sections.\nCase: a Codex `exec` body runs `cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md` and the run then writes into the packet's review folder; `workflowPath` says `command`, but `startState.started` is false, `takenLoop` returns null, and `unsafe` stays false even though the loop began without its lock/init.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The area implements the packet's command-surfacing measurement, not a spec behavior; the offer fields and the scorer are checked against their own README claims. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | The parent packet holds no checklist; no checked item names this area. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition owns `accuracy-runner`. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | The Codex session reader and the six-runtime tool tables were read; live per-runtime proof stays phase 007's. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3 with the README claims. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3 if reached. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Producer `replayOffer` / `parseOffer`: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:70-146`.\n- Producer consumer #1 `backfillRunLog`: `command-offer.mjs:486-499`.\n- Producer consumer #2 `run-command-behaviour.mjs` `appendRunLine`: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187` (read-only context; unchanged since pass three).\n- Consumer `offerOf` / `scoreRun`: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1464-1473,1533-1541`.\n- Shell reader and its consumers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:643-693,718-748,775-813`.\n- Codex reader's `input` body: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs:99-113`.\n- Tests: `command-offer.vitest.ts:98-113,280-302,305-350`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:190-275,2199-2252`.\n- Shared docs: `README.md:58-72,123,187`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Holdout rows: read by id, split and row type only; no holdout prompt text was printed. The fit/decline counts are handled in iteration 2.\n- An old run line with no `offeredAs`: the scorer deliberately keeps it in `offered` so a historical log is not re-read as no offer. That is not the same as a new line never carrying the field, which is finding 1.\n- A `COMMAND:` line naming a command twice: `commandLines` counts the command once per line and `repeatedCommands` counts the duplicate; not re-raised here.\n- A shell command with a redirect: `redirectTargets` respects quoting; the `cat notes.md > SKILL.md` case is a write, not a read.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `normalize` reads a Codex `exec_command` call through both `command` and `cmd`, and a bare `exec` body through `exec_command`/`cmd` or every string; the tests pin both shapes.\n- `SHELL_READERS` no longer includes `rg` or `grep`; a search cannot count as a load.\n- `cd` in the same command resolves a bare document name against that folder, including a quoted folder with a trailing slash.\n- `offerOf` excludes a partner-side command when the line actually carries `offeredAs: 'partner'`; the unit test pins that branch.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A Codex body string that is not a command but names a document.** The every-string fallback only runs when no `cmd:` literal exists, and the test's list form is the intended shape; no real body in the area names a workflow document from a non-command string. Deferred as a hardening note, not a finding.\n- **`rg`/`grep` counted as a load.** Removed from `SHELL_READERS`; the shell reader also ignores a search's printed path.\n- **A `cd` that changes the folder for later commands.** The folder is carried across `&&`/`;` parts; the tests cover the quoted trailing-slash form.\n- **A read after the first write still counted as followed.** `followedBeforeWrite` compares the event position to the boundary; the existing negative tests hold.\n- **A `COMMAND:` line naming another command.** `offerSeenIn` filters through `namesCommand`; the declined-other-command test holds.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: the capture's fit/decline rows and the live holdout guard\n- Reason: the fit tally is the new measurement for refusals and questions, and the brief asks whether those rows can still carry or start a mutating command; the holdout guard must be checked against the live capture, not only the committed baseline\n- Rotation status: correctness complete; security next\n- Required evidence: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:560-700`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-267`, `command-routing-baseline.json:1961-1984`\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-4`, pass four)\\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Dimension: D1 Correctness, first pass over the area changed since pass three\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Budget profile: verify (12 review actions)\\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: pass-four review of command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area. Read `review-brief-4.txt` first; review the files whose area is `accuracy-runner` plus shared docs; check the six runtimes, whether a refusal/question/mention can attach or start a mutating command, whether the transcript scorer counts a load/followed step/offer that did not happen (Codex exec bodies, rg/grep, heredocs, cd, partner-side commands, paired arms, Wilson ranges), holdout hygiene, and docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text.\\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it read the two pass-four producer changes (`command-offer.mjs` and the `4a622e419f` offer field) against their consumer (`score-command-transcripts.mjs`), then read the `a1c31b6f38` Codex/heredoc/`cd` reader and its tests. It found the partner-side offer field that is computed and then dropped before any run line reaches the scorer, a heredoc delimiter the new shell reader leaves in the command stream, and a shell read the new path counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop. Holdout rows were counted only; no holdout prompt text was printed.\\n- `steer.md`: absent before this iteration; no lead rulings to apply.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:52-80,99-147,486-499`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1177-1190` (read-only producer context; unchanged since pass three)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:643-693,718-748,913-926,975-990,1430-1438,1464-1474`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:58-72,123,187`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:73-113,305-350`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:177-275,2199-2252`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (ids, splits and row types only; no holdout prompt text)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **The partner-side offer field is computed and then dropped by both offer writers** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:486` -- `parseOffer` and `replayOffer` return `offeredAs` (`head` or `partner`), and the scorer's `offerOf` uses it to keep a command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head out of `offered` (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1464-1473`). No writer persists that field. `backfillRunLog` copies only `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled` into the new line (`command-offer.mjs:490-497`). The live runner's `appendRunLine` copies only `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` from the same replay (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187`). A real backfilled or live run line therefore has no `offeredAs`, and `offerOf` reads `undefined !== 'partner'` as `offered: true`. The README says \\\"Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`\\\" (`README.md:123`) and separately lists the output fields without it (`README.md:187`), so the docs disagree with each other and with both writers.\\nFinding class: correctness / cross-consumer\\nScope proof: `rg -n \\\"offeredAs\\\"` over the runtime shows the only producers are `failedOffer`, `parseOffer` and `replayOffer`, the only consumer is `offerOf`, and both write paths that call `replayOffer` select fields without it. `command-offer.vitest.ts:337-350`'s replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so the backfill test cannot catch the drop.\\nAffected surface hints: `command-offer.mjs` `backfillRunLog`; `run-command-behaviour.mjs` `appendRunLine`; `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `offerOf`; README \\\"Attribution on every run line\\\" and \\\"Backfill a finished log\\\".\\nCase: a run whose head is `Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-code 0.95/0.12 vs sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.82/0.12 pass.` gets `offeredAs: 'partner'` from `replayOffer`; the line written by the runner or a backfill has no `offeredAs`; the scorer counts `/create:manual-testing-playbook` as `offered` and leaves `offeredAsPartner` at 0, so `startedOfOffered` and `followedOffered` treat a command the head showed on the partner side as an offer the head made.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The partner-side offer marker is added by parseOffer/replayOffer but is not copied into any run line by either producer, so the scorer's partner-side exclusion never fires on a real log.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:70-81\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:486-497\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1464-1473\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:187\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Searched every runtime file for another writer of offeredAs (none); checked whether run-command-behaviour spreads the whole replay object (it selects two fields); checked whether the scorer can infer the partner side from offeredCommand alone (the same string can be head or partner); checked whether the backfill test's stub returns offeredAs (it does not).\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"The field could be intended only for the scorer's unit tests and for a future producer, in which case the README claim and the scorer's read are the defects rather than the writers.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.95,\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"If every run log is normalized to add offeredAs before scoring, or the scorer derives the partner side from a stored head, this becomes a P2 documentation cleanup.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:647` -- `HEREDOC_BODY` matches a delimiter with `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*` only. A quoted delimiter with a hyphen, such as `END-SCRIPT`, is not matched, so the body stays in the command stream and `shellReadTargets` parses its lines as commands. A body line that names a workflow document then counts as a load the run never performed. The only heredoc tests use `EOF` (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:2222-2223`).\\nFinding class: correctness / measurement\\nScope proof: the regex is the only heredoc filter, `shellReadTargets` is the only shell reader, and both `followedBeforeWrite` and `ownerLoadedBeforeWrite` consume its targets. No test uses a delimiter outside the identifier grammar.\\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `HEREDOC_BODY`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` heredoc cases.\\nCase: a Codex or Claude shell step runs `python3 - <<'END-SCRIPT'` with a body line `cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` and then writes; the body is data, but `shellReadTargets` returns the `SKILL.md` target and `workflowPath` reports `skill` although the file was never opened.\\n\\n2. **A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:913` -- The pass-four shell-read support is wired into `followedBeforeWrite` (`:734-736`) and `ownerLoadedBeforeWrite` (`:793`), but `readDocument` still accepts only `read` and `skill` events (`:916-923`). `startState` therefore reports `started: false` for a Codex run that `cat`s the command document, and `takenLoop` (`:1430-1438`) cannot name a loop opened the same way, so a deep-loop run that reads its document through the shell and writes without its init is not marked unsafe.\\nFinding class: correctness / measurement\\nScope proof: `readDocument` is the single start/loop detector; the new shell readers are the only way a Codex `exec` body becomes a load; no test combines a shell read with `startState` or `takenLoop`.\\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `readDocument`, `startState`, `takenLoop`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` start and loop sections.\\nCase: a Codex `exec` body runs `cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md` and the run then writes into the packet's review folder; `workflowPath` says `command`, but `startState.started` is false, `takenLoop` returns null, and `unsafe` stays false even though the loop began without its lock/init.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The area implements the packet's command-surfacing measurement, not a spec behavior; the offer fields and the scorer are checked against their own README claims. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | The parent packet holds no checklist; no checked item names this area. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition owns `accuracy-runner`. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | The Codex session reader and the six-runtime tool tables were read; live per-runtime proof stays phase 007's. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3 with the README claims. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3 if reached. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Producer `replayOffer` / `parseOffer`: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:70-146`.\\n- Producer consumer #1 `backfillRunLog`: `command-offer.mjs:486-499`.\\n- Producer consumer #2 `run-command-behaviour.mjs` `appendRunLine`: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187` (read-only context; unchanged since pass three).\\n- Consumer `offerOf` / `scoreRun`: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1464-1473,1533-1541`.\\n- Shell reader and its consumers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:643-693,718-748,775-813`.\\n- Codex reader's `input` body: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs:99-113`.\\n- Tests: `command-offer.vitest.ts:98-113,280-302,305-350`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:190-275,2199-2252`.\\n- Shared docs: `README.md:58-72,123,187`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Holdout rows: read by id, split and row type only; no holdout prompt text was printed. The fit/decline counts are handled in iteration 2.\\n- An old run line with no `offeredAs`: the scorer deliberately keeps it in `offered` so a historical log is not re-read as no offer. That is not the same as a new line never carrying the field, which is finding 1.\\n- A `COMMAND:` line naming a command twice: `commandLines` counts the command once per line and `repeatedCommands` counts the duplicate; not re-raised here.\\n- A shell command with a redirect: `redirectTargets` respects quoting; the `cat notes.md > SKILL.md` case is a write, not a read.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `normalize` reads a Codex `exec_command` call through both `command` and `cmd`, and a bare `exec` body through `exec_command`/`cmd` or every string; the tests pin both shapes.\\n- `SHELL_READERS` no longer includes `rg` or `grep`; a search cannot count as a load.\\n- `cd` in the same command resolves a bare document name against that folder, including a quoted folder with a trailing slash.\\n- `offerOf` excludes a partner-side command when the line actually carries `offeredAs: 'partner'`; the unit test pins that branch.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A Codex body string that is not a command but names a document.** The every-string fallback only runs when no `cmd:` literal exists, and the test's list form is the intended shape; no real body in the area names a workflow document from a non-command string. Deferred as a hardening note, not a finding.\\n- **`rg`/`grep` counted as a load.** Removed from `SHELL_READERS`; the shell reader also ignores a search's printed path.\\n- **A `cd` that changes the folder for later commands.** The folder is carried across `&&`/`;` parts; the tests cover the quoted trailing-slash form.\\n- **A read after the first write still counted as followed.** `followedBeforeWrite` compares the event position to the boundary; the existing negative tests hold.\\n- **A `COMMAND:` line naming another command.** `offerSeenIn` filters through `namesCommand`; the declined-other-command test holds.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: the capture's fit/decline rows and the live holdout guard\\n- Reason: the fit tally is the new measurement for refusals and questions, and the brief asks whether those rows can still carry or start a mutating command; the holdout guard must be checked against the live capture, not only the committed baseline\\n- Rotation status: correctness complete; security next\\n- Required evidence: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:560-700`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-267`, `command-routing-baseline.json:1961-1984`\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670594950,"end":1794670628011}}}}
