{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670714256,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab5d1e4002p1E0Gb9ViPLSWT","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab5c0bc001PLd2T20hWxzcsm","type":"tool","id":"call_7fb56c3713114dedb2faab0d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \"adds the offer\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -64,14 +64,17 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n-[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n+- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n+- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n-[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n+- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \"adds the offer\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\\n- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \\\"adds the offer\\\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670711268,"end":1794670714256}}}}
