{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670832245,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab7a658002zatvOelH0Mli2i","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab79067001kdKFjyGWaGBwoh","type":"tool","id":"call_863269061ac24c15a5af23ac","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '20,75p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md; echo \"---next---\"; grep -n \"ANCHOR:next-focus\" -A8 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin` or `doctor-docs` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n- Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n- Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n- Not running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage; runners are audited by reading\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n- `maxIterations=4` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n- Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 2\n- P2 (Suggestions): 3\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n---next---\n149:<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150-## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151-- Dimension: traceability - Focus area: whether the new fit/stage counts are held to the committed baseline, and whether the README's new claims match the code - Reason: the safety counts are now reported but not ratcheted; the README's `offeredAs` claim already disagrees with both writers (iteration 1), so the remaining docs and the attached-metrics block need a baseline check - Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability next - Required evidence: `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-282`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:726-776`, `README.md:118-123,187` Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n152-\n153:<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n154-\n155----\n156-\n157-## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158-\n159-- Pass three closed at `0cdc9fa3ef`; HEAD is `400c90e158`; the area diff is six files, 2,392 insertions and 48 deletions\n160-- The area's current state is the commit pair `4a622e419f` (fit rows, workflow block, offer `offeredAs`) and `a1c31b6f38` (Codex shell steps, heredoc/cd, partner offers)\n161-- Baseline `command-routing-baseline.json` was captured at SHA `60968af043`, pinned date `2026-10-11`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin` or `doctor-docs` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n- Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n- Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n- Not running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage; runners are audited by reading\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n- `maxIterations=4` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n- Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 2\n- P2 (Suggestions): 3\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n---next---\n149: