{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670996751,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab9d8a7001nNb7NBiX0s816L","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dab97f9f001R1d7aoe8wD7wSL","type":"tool","id":"call_142181eb4c3b435a9f4790cb","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-4`, pass four)\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Dimension: D4 Maintainability, plus the terminal adjudication replay\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (10 review actions)\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: pass-four review of command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area; close the coverage map, re-read every active finding's evidence, and keep the terminal record honest about the loop stopping at the configured cap.\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it read the summary's key space around `unscored` and `paired`, then re-read the two active P1s and the four earlier P2s at their cited lines. It found the `paired` key collision and the dead `workflow.unscoredOnly` field, confirmed the active findings still describe the code on disk, and recorded that the loop's fourth iteration is also its last configured iteration. Holdout rows were counted only.\n- `steer.md`: absent before this iteration; no lead rulings to apply.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1345-1405,1600-1705,1742-1815,1856-1957`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1610-1770`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:486-499` (active P1 re-read)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595-607,666-677` (active P1 re-read)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-282` (active P2 re-read)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:122-123` (active P2/P1 doc lines)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (ids, splits and row types only; no holdout prompt text)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. The iteration-1 offered-field P1 and the iteration-2 fit-gate P1 remain active; both were re-read at their cited lines and still describe the code on disk.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **An arm named `paired` is silently hidden or overwritten by the summary's pair block** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1911` -- The summary reserves the `unscored` key for its own count (`RESERVED_ARM` at `:1347-1352`), but `paired` is not reserved. `project` writes every arm into `block[arm]` (`:1869-1871`), then writes the comparison into `block.paired` (`:1892`). `writeSummary` skips any arm named `paired` (`:1911`). A run-log line whose `arm` is `paired` is therefore absent from the text summary, and with `--pair` its counts are replaced by the comparison object.\nFinding class: maintainability / reserved-key collision\nScope proof: `RESERVED_ARM` is the only reserved arm label; `rg -n \"paired\"` shows `project` and `writeSummary` use the key without a guard; the documented arm names are `pre`, `post` and `g2`, but `--arm` accepts an operator string and the code already defends the other reserved word.\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `armOf`, `project`, `writeSummary`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` pair cases.\nCase: a run log line `{\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"rowId\":\"cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01\",\"arm\":\"paired\",\"exit\":0,\"locator\":{...}}` is read; `armOf` returns `paired`; the text summary prints no `paired:` arm line, and `--pair pre,post` replaces the arm's block with `{from,to,rows,gained,lost,...}` so its counts disappear.\n\n2. **The workflow block's `unscoredOnly` count is never incremented** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1629` -- `newTally` initializes `workflow.unscoredOnly` to 0 and `tallyBlock` adds it to `tally.unscored` (`:1698`), but no code writes it. Every `workflow.unscored` is therefore the arm's `tally.unscored` alone, and the field reads as a separate category that never exists.\nFinding class: maintainability / dead field\nScope proof: `grep -n \"unscoredOnly\"` finds only the declaration and the read; no increment appears in `addScored` or `summarize`.\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `newTally`/`tallyBlock`; README workflow block.\nCase: an arm with one unscored run reports `workflow.unscored: 1`; the `unscoredOnly` term contributes 0, so a maintainer who wires a separate count or reads the field as \"unscored only for the workflow\" gets the arm total, not a distinct value.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The area is a measurement harness; no normative spec threshold names these keys. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | The parent packet holds no checklist. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition owns the area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | The summary key space is runtime-independent; live per-runtime proof stays phase 007's. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | README rows checked through iteration 3; the `paired` key claim is finding 1's doc side. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook scenario names these keys. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Reserved arm handling: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1345-1352`.\n- Summary projection: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1856-1900`.\n- Text writer: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1902-1957`.\n- Workflow tally: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1600-1640,1688-1735`.\n- Pair tests: `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1610-1770`.\n- Active P1/P2 evidence re-read: `command-offer.mjs:486-499`; `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595-607,666-677`; `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-282`; `README.md:122-123`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The `paired` collision needs an operator-supplied arm label; the runner's documented sets are `pre`, `post` and `g2`, so the reach is a mistyped or deliberately named arm, not a default run.\n- The `paired` block is only written when the two arms share at least one owned row; the reserved-key bug exists with or without a pair because `writeSummary` skips the arm name unconditionally.\n- The `unscoredOnly` term is zero in every block; it never changes a rate, so the defect is clarity rather than a wrong count.\n- The active P1s were not downgraded: `offeredAs` is still absent from both writers, and the fit `carried` is still only checked against `total`.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `armOf` files `unscored` under `unknown`, so the one reserved word the code does defend cannot overwrite the runtime's `unscored` count.\n- `project` computes `largestRuns` from run counts, and `armIncomplete` is correct for a runtime that ran fewer turns.\n- The pair comparison counts only the intersection of the two arms' `pairRows`, and the one-arm case produces no block.\n- The active P1 evidence is unchanged: both writers still omit `offeredAs`, and the capture still continues before the false-offer tally.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A new correctness or security finding in the summary key space.** The `paired` collision is a naming/reservation gap; the counts themselves are correct when the arm name is not reserved.\n- **The iteration-1 P1 is stale.** Re-read `command-offer.mjs:486-499`; both writers still omit `offeredAs`.\n- **The iteration-2 P1 is stale.** Re-read `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595-607,666-677` and the baseline's `fit.decline.carried: 8`; the rows still leave the false-offer tally.\n- **The `noOwner` pair exclusion is a counting bug.** It is the documented `pairRows` rule; the README's wording is the iteration-3 finding, not a second defect.\n- **A holdout leak in this iteration.** The summary keys and the new findings name no holdout prompt; the fit and stage blocks stay counts-only.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none (maintainability is the last configured dimension)\n- Focus area: terminal synthesis and the active-finding replay\n- Reason: the loop reaches `maxIterations=4` after this iteration; the next step is the synthesis report and the closeout event, not another dispatch. The two active P1s keep the verdict CONDITIONAL; the seven P2s are advisories.\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; no new dimension remains\n- Required evidence: the findings registry, all four iteration files and deltas, and the reducer's final state\n- Recovery note: the run did not reach a legal graph-backed convergence; the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`, and the report must say so.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-4`, pass four)\\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Dimension: D4 Maintainability, plus the terminal adjudication replay\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (10 review actions)\\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: pass-four review of command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area; close the coverage map, re-read every active finding's evidence, and keep the terminal record honest about the loop stopping at the configured cap.\\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it read the summary's key space around `unscored` and `paired`, then re-read the two active P1s and the four earlier P2s at their cited lines. It found the `paired` key collision and the dead `workflow.unscoredOnly` field, confirmed the active findings still describe the code on disk, and recorded that the loop's fourth iteration is also its last configured iteration. Holdout rows were counted only.\\n- `steer.md`: absent before this iteration; no lead rulings to apply.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1345-1405,1600-1705,1742-1815,1856-1957`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1610-1770`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:486-499` (active P1 re-read)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595-607,666-677` (active P1 re-read)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-282` (active P2 re-read)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:122-123` (active P2/P1 doc lines)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (ids, splits and row types only; no holdout prompt text)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. The iteration-1 offered-field P1 and the iteration-2 fit-gate P1 remain active; both were re-read at their cited lines and still describe the code on disk.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **An arm named `paired` is silently hidden or overwritten by the summary's pair block** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1911` -- The summary reserves the `unscored` key for its own count (`RESERVED_ARM` at `:1347-1352`), but `paired` is not reserved. `project` writes every arm into `block[arm]` (`:1869-1871`), then writes the comparison into `block.paired` (`:1892`). `writeSummary` skips any arm named `paired` (`:1911`). A run-log line whose `arm` is `paired` is therefore absent from the text summary, and with `--pair` its counts are replaced by the comparison object.\\nFinding class: maintainability / reserved-key collision\\nScope proof: `RESERVED_ARM` is the only reserved arm label; `rg -n \\\"paired\\\"` shows `project` and `writeSummary` use the key without a guard; the documented arm names are `pre`, `post` and `g2`, but `--arm` accepts an operator string and the code already defends the other reserved word.\\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `armOf`, `project`, `writeSummary`; `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` pair cases.\\nCase: a run log line `{\\\"runtime\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"rowId\\\":\\\"cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01\\\",\\\"arm\\\":\\\"paired\\\",\\\"exit\\\":0,\\\"locator\\\":{...}}` is read; `armOf` returns `paired`; the text summary prints no `paired:` arm line, and `--pair pre,post` replaces the arm's block with `{from,to,rows,gained,lost,...}` so its counts disappear.\\n\\n2. **The workflow block's `unscoredOnly` count is never incremented** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1629` -- `newTally` initializes `workflow.unscoredOnly` to 0 and `tallyBlock` adds it to `tally.unscored` (`:1698`), but no code writes it. Every `workflow.unscored` is therefore the arm's `tally.unscored` alone, and the field reads as a separate category that never exists.\\nFinding class: maintainability / dead field\\nScope proof: `grep -n \\\"unscoredOnly\\\"` finds only the declaration and the read; no increment appears in `addScored` or `summarize`.\\nAffected surface hints: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `newTally`/`tallyBlock`; README workflow block.\\nCase: an arm with one unscored run reports `workflow.unscored: 1`; the `unscoredOnly` term contributes 0, so a maintainer who wires a separate count or reads the field as \\\"unscored only for the workflow\\\" gets the arm total, not a distinct value.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The area is a measurement harness; no normative spec threshold names these keys. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | The parent packet holds no checklist. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition owns the area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | The summary key space is runtime-independent; live per-runtime proof stays phase 007's. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | README rows checked through iteration 3; the `paired` key claim is finding 1's doc side. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook scenario names these keys. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Reserved arm handling: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1345-1352`.\\n- Summary projection: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1856-1900`.\\n- Text writer: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1902-1957`.\\n- Workflow tally: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1600-1640,1688-1735`.\\n- Pair tests: `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1610-1770`.\\n- Active P1/P2 evidence re-read: `command-offer.mjs:486-499`; `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595-607,666-677`; `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-282`; `README.md:122-123`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The `paired` collision needs an operator-supplied arm label; the runner's documented sets are `pre`, `post` and `g2`, so the reach is a mistyped or deliberately named arm, not a default run.\\n- The `paired` block is only written when the two arms share at least one owned row; the reserved-key bug exists with or without a pair because `writeSummary` skips the arm name unconditionally.\\n- The `unscoredOnly` term is zero in every block; it never changes a rate, so the defect is clarity rather than a wrong count.\\n- The active P1s were not downgraded: `offeredAs` is still absent from both writers, and the fit `carried` is still only checked against `total`.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `armOf` files `unscored` under `unknown`, so the one reserved word the code does defend cannot overwrite the runtime's `unscored` count.\\n- `project` computes `largestRuns` from run counts, and `armIncomplete` is correct for a runtime that ran fewer turns.\\n- The pair comparison counts only the intersection of the two arms' `pairRows`, and the one-arm case produces no block.\\n- The active P1 evidence is unchanged: both writers still omit `offeredAs`, and the capture still continues before the false-offer tally.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A new correctness or security finding in the summary key space.** The `paired` collision is a naming/reservation gap; the counts themselves are correct when the arm name is not reserved.\\n- **The iteration-1 P1 is stale.** Re-read `command-offer.mjs:486-499`; both writers still omit `offeredAs`.\\n- **The iteration-2 P1 is stale.** Re-read `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595-607,666-677` and the baseline's `fit.decline.carried: 8`; the rows still leave the false-offer tally.\\n- **The `noOwner` pair exclusion is a counting bug.** It is the documented `pairRows` rule; the README's wording is the iteration-3 finding, not a second defect.\\n- **A holdout leak in this iteration.** The summary keys and the new findings name no holdout prompt; the fit and stage blocks stay counts-only.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none (maintainability is the last configured dimension)\\n- Focus area: terminal synthesis and the active-finding replay\\n- Reason: the loop reaches `maxIterations=4` after this iteration; the next step is the synthesis report and the closeout event, not another dispatch. The two active P1s keep the verdict CONDITIONAL; the seven P2s are advisories.\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; no new dimension remains\\n- Required evidence: the findings registry, all four iteration files and deltas, and the reducer's final state\\n- Recovery note: the run did not reach a legal graph-backed convergence; the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`, and the report must say so.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670975143,"end":1794670996751}}}}
