{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794671082459,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"id":"prt_1dabb7bdb001CHCnt6kAOkldqT","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dabb6a80001QbzFP7vuzjip2l","type":"step-start","snapshot":"408ac489a810f77d9713a3844c8e0bc64fcc5cfe"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794671089360,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dabb7ef8002y5pmI5B2ZrqGeW","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dabb6a80001QbzFP7vuzjip2l","type":"tool","id":"call_04ea6efe1fcc47e4b383cfd3","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n- Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\n- Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\n- Comparing the slice file's baseline comparisons with the new attached-metrics blocks found that the stage and fit counts are invariant-tested but never baseline-pinned (iteration 3).\n- Treating the summary as one key space found that `unscored` is reserved but `paired` is not, and that `workflow.unscoredOnly` is never written (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \"adds the offer\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\n- Reading the slice test's holdout check by name looked sufficient; only tracing its `baseline` binding showed it never reads the live maps (iteration 2).\n- The new stage tests look like a ratchet because they assert partitions and fixed totals; only tracing which object they read showed the baseline is never consulted (iteration 3).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n- Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\n- Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \"adds the offer\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\n- Reading the slice test's holdout check by name looked sufficient; only tracing its `baseline` binding showed it never reads the live maps (iteration 2).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -70,15 +70,18 @@\n - Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n - Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n - Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\n - Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\n+- Comparing the slice file's baseline comparisons with the new attached-metrics blocks found that the stage and fit counts are invariant-tested but never baseline-pinned (iteration 3).\n+- Treating the summary as one key space found that `unscored` is reserved but `paired` is not, and that `workflow.unscoredOnly` is never written (iteration 4).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n - Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n - The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \"adds the offer\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\n - Reading the slice test's holdout check by name looked sufficient; only tracing its `baseline` binding showed it never reads the live maps (iteration 2).\n+- The new stage tests look like a ratchet because they assert partitions and fixed totals; only tracing which object they read showed the baseline is never consulted (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\\n- Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\\n- Comparing the slice file's baseline comparisons with the new attached-metrics blocks found that the stage and fit counts are invariant-tested but never baseline-pinned (iteration 3).\\n- Treating the summary as one key space found that `unscored` is reserved but `paired` is not, and that `workflow.unscoredOnly` is never written (iteration 4).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\\n- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \\\"adds the offer\\\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the slice test's holdout check by name looked sufficient; only tracing its `baseline` binding showed it never reads the live maps (iteration 2).\\n- The new stage tests look like a ratchet because they assert partitions and fixed totals; only tracing which object they read showed the baseline is never consulted (iteration 3).\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\\n- Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\\n- The backfill test's replay stub returns no `offeredAs`, so its \\\"adds the offer\\\" assertion could not catch the drop (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the slice test's holdout check by name looked sufficient; only tracing its `baseline` binding showed it never reads the live maps (iteration 2).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794671083256,"end":1794671089360}}}}
