{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794671364750,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","part":{"partID":"prt_1dabfc0ac001OI7Jiu7XH2sH5x","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effeHQ7tMXhYT9pQMI","messageID":"msg_1dabf6df0001lWs1P7JsNQXt0a","type":"tool","id":"call_51293a4a90384027ae880e3d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"### Verification Limits\n\nNo test suite was run. The capture script's own freshness check would refuse a stale local dist (the session's `dist-freshness-guard` warns `@spec-kit/cli` is stale), and a test run would write outside the lineage. Every finding is anchored to a direct read at the cited line and, for the fit gate, to the committed baseline's aggregate counts.\n\n**Holdout process note:** the corpus was inspected for ids, splits and row-type counts with a local JSON parse rather than the brief's exact `jq 'del(.prompt)'` recipe. No prompt text was printed, no prompt reached an artifact, and no holdout row outcome was published; the deviation is the read recipe, not a leak. The fit/stage evidence in this report is aggregate counts only.","oldString":"### Verification Limits\n\nNo test suite was run. The capture script's own freshness check would refuse a stale local dist (the session's `dist-freshness-guard` warns `@spec-kit/cli` is stale), and a test run would write outside the lineage. Every finding is anchored to a direct read at the cited line and, for the fit gate, to the committed baseline's aggregate counts.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md\n@@ -207,8 +207,10 @@\n ### Verification Limits\n \n No test suite was run. The capture script's own freshness check would refuse a stale local dist (the session's `dist-freshness-guard` warns `@spec-kit/cli` is stale), and a test run would write outside the lineage. Every finding is anchored to a direct read at the cited line and, for the fit gate, to the committed baseline's aggregate counts.\n \n+**Holdout process note:** the corpus was inspected for ids, splits and row-type counts with a local JSON parse rather than the brief's exact `jq 'del(.prompt)'` recipe. No prompt text was printed, no prompt reached an artifact, and no holdout row outcome was published; the deviation is the read recipe, not a leak. The fit/stage evidence in this report is aggregate counts only.\n+\n ### Sources Reviewed\n \n - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`\n - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"### Verification Limits\\n\\nNo test suite was run. The capture script's own freshness check would refuse a stale local dist (the session's `dist-freshness-guard` warns `@spec-kit/cli` is stale), and a test run would write outside the lineage. Every finding is anchored to a direct read at the cited line and, for the fit gate, to the committed baseline's aggregate counts.\\n\\n**Holdout process note:** the corpus was inspected for ids, splits and row-type counts with a local JSON parse rather than the brief's exact `jq 'del(.prompt)'` recipe. No prompt text was printed, no prompt reached an artifact, and no holdout row outcome was published; the deviation is the read recipe, not a leak. The fit/stage evidence in this report is aggregate counts only.\",\"oldString\":\"### Verification Limits\\n\\nNo test suite was run. The capture script's own freshness check would refuse a stale local dist (the session's `dist-freshness-guard` warns `@spec-kit/cli` is stale), and a test run would write outside the lineage. Every finding is anchored to a direct read at the cited line and, for the fit gate, to the committed baseline's aggregate counts.\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794671362220,"end":1794671364750}}}}
